+## 4. Fix-delta between the two repos (the actionable finding)
+
+- **supremeai-open** `core/messaging/event_bus.py` (~:390–405): the telemetry forward is wrapped — `try: from monitoring import track_exception; track_exception(...) except Exception as exc: logger.warning("[EventBus] telemetry forward unavailable …")` with an explicit anti-suppression contract comment (Bengali, cites live 2026-10-29 evidence and "update_failed since 2026-10-24"). This hardening is why the open mirror cannot reproduce the boot-kill.
+- **supremeai-core** `core/messaging/event_bus.py:388`: the same import is **unguarded inside emit()**, and `core/errors/error_bus.py:57` calls `error_event_bus.emit(event)` unguarded inside its own `except` handler — so the reporting path replaces the original settings failure with an ImportError and kills the process.
+- This cycle additionally hardens **supremeai-open** `core/errors/error_bus.py` (both sync/async wrappers now guard the emit call — defense in depth at the outermost layer; smoke-tested: original exception preserved when emit raises).
+
+## 5. Remedies (outside this agent's envelope — for the verdict/admin plane)
